"Restrict the `CustomOidcRequestFilter` filter to OIDC tenants `tenant-one` "
"and `tenant-two`."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"An OIDC response filter can be restricted to the specific OIDC endpoint or "
"endpoints with the `quarkus.oidc.common.OidcEndpoint` annotation."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tenant resolution for OIDC web-app applications"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Tenant resolution for the OIDC `web-app` applications must be done at least "
"3 times during an authorization code flow, when the OIDC tenant-specific "
"configuration affects how each of the following steps is run."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Step 1: Unauthenticated user accesses an endpoint and is redirected to OIDC "
"provider"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When an unauthenticated user accesses a secured path, the user is redirected "
"to the OIDC provider to authenticate and the tenant configuration is used to "
"build the redirect URI."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All the static and dynamic tenant resolution options listed in the <<static-"
"tenant-resolution>> and <<tenant-config-resolver>> sections can be used to "
"resolve a tenant."
msgstr ""

msgid "Step 2: The user is redirected back to the endpoint"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"After the provider authentication, the user is redirected back to the "
"Quarkus endpoint and the tenant configuration is used to complete the "
"authorization code flow."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"All the static and dynamic tenant resolution options listed in the <<static-"
"tenant-resolution>> and <<tenant-config-resolver>> sections can be used to "
"resolve a tenant. Before the tenant resolution begins, the authorization "
"code flow `state cookie` is used to set the already resolved tenant "
"configuration id as a RoutingContext `tenant-id` attribute: both custom "
"dynamic `TenantConfigResolver` and static `TenantResolver` tenant resolvers "
"can check it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Step 3: Authenticated user accesses the secured path using the session "
"cookie"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The tenant configuration determines how the session cookie is verified and "
"refreshed. Before the tenant resolution begins, the authorization code flow "
"`session cookie` is used to set the already resolved tenant configuration id "
"as a RoutingContext `tenant-id` attribute: both custom dynamic "
"`TenantConfigResolver` and static `TenantResolver` tenant resolvers can "
"check it."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
